1
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:17,380
Chief Liu,

2
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,700
preliminary estimates show

3
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,300
we need at least 80 officers for surveillance.

4
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,560
Our Economic Crime team is short-handed.

5
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,900
Criminal Investigation has several cases

6
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:28,060
under investigation.

7
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,520
We can't drop any of them.

8
00:00:30,180 --> 00:00:31,460
Stop complaining.

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,020
If there's a problem, solve it.

10
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:34,280
Just now,

11
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,580
Comrade Geng Qing spoke with me.

12
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:38,420
I think his ideas are sound.

13
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,700
We must uphold the philosophy of

14
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,320
investigating a case to reform an entire sector.

15
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,700
Investigating cases

16
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,000
isn't just about finding who took bribes

17
00:00:46,080 --> 00:00:47,140
or who pulled strings,

18
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,820
or catching a few corrupt officials.

19
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,240
More importantly,

20
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,820
it's about using these cases

21
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,580
to plug loopholes in the bidding system.

22
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:56,160
What is the ultimate purpose

23
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,440
of all our Party and government organs?

24
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:59,720
Is it just to show report cards to the public?

25
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:00,680
Yes,

26
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:01,640
but not just that.

27
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,280
Is it to uncover corrupt networks?

28
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:05,660
Of course it is,

29
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:06,960
but that's far from enough.

30
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:09,840
We must take precautions and sound alarms

31
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,200
to prevent minor errors from becoming disasters.

32
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,220
Through these investigations,

33
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:15,560
we must let the public see

34
00:01:15,780 --> 00:01:18,260
our Party's people-centered stance,

35
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:21,360
so they support our Party even more

36
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,880
and have greater trust in the government.

37
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:27,040
Only then can we strengthen our governing foundation.

38
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:29,920
If the suspects feign moves

39
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,880
and create diversions,

40
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:32,340
and we simply stop here,

41
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:35,920
it'll be a disgrace to everyone here.

42
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,380
It would be a dereliction of duty

43
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:40,100
that our team can never wash away.

44
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,220
Comrades,

45
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:43,820
no matter what hidden currents

46
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,880
or obstacles lie ahead,

47
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,860
we have no reason to back down!

48
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:51,340
I agree with Comrade Geng Qing's proposal.

49
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,100
Extend our frontline.

50
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:54,940
Except for special circumstances,

51
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:57,460
initiate project confidentiality protocols.

52
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,120
Our task force will go all out.

53
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:02,060
Economic Crime will fully cooperate.

54
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,120
Criminal Investigation will fully cooperate.

55
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:07,140
Every municipal department will coordinate.

56
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,540
I await your good news.

57
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,140
I need the original number to reach Du Qingbo.

58
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,380
Here's the written permit.

59
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:17,300
Understood, Team Leader.

60
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,140
Sign here.

61
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:24,780
Secretary Luo really has great vision.

62
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:26,820
Yeah, I think so too.

63
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,300
Don't flatter yourself.

64
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:29,380
You don't have those guts.

65
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:31,660
Hey,

66
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:34,840
I was the one who went to Secretary Luo.

67
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:38,040
I mean the vision to see the big picture.

68
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:44,940
What are you laughing at?

69
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,240
What do you think?

70
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,100
Right now, the police

71
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,960
have set up comprehensive surveillance.

72
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:03,620
We can't just sit on our hands either.

73
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,360
Lu'an Group's project

74
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,820
is a key provincial engineering project.

75
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:10,000
With projects like this,

76
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:12,800
criminals are more likely to push their luck

77
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:14,000
and take desperate risks.

78
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,440
Then let's simply

79
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:16,980
take the initiative

80
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,800
and deter them at critical stages,

81
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:21,040
forcing them to slip up.

82
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,320
Understood.

83
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,700
What projects are at the trading center these days?

84
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:27,160
Secretary Luo, Team Leader Geng,

85
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:28,720
there are six projects in total.

86
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,060
The largest investment is 970,000,

87
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:33,420
renovating the Guangming Community fitness area.

88
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,500
Winning a bid always involves the experts.

89
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,820
Then let's simply

90
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:38,380
call in all the experts for questioning.

91
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:39,400
The police won't be involved.

92
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,160
Liu Rong will be in full charge.

93
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,320
Understood.

94
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:53,260
Please, have a seat.

95
00:03:56,500 --> 00:03:58,220
You must have made a mistake.

96
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,780
I have very strong principles.

97
00:04:00,020 --> 00:04:01,220
I always have.

98
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:05,260
From when you got the notice this morning,

99
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:06,540
please go over it one more time.

100
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,860
I've said it three times already!

101
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:11,540
Please believe me.

102
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:13,380
I'm a veteran Party member, too!

103
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:18,500
I just couldn't resist the temptation.

104
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:21,180
The expert evaluation fee

105
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:23,180
is 150 an hour.

106
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:25,260
Just putting in a word

107
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:26,260
and lifting a finger,

108
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:28,600
and that's an easy 10,000!

109
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,560
That bid...

110
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:32,820
I really wasn't involved in it.

111
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:33,180
I...

112
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,840
My target...

113
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,440
...was next door.

114
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:41,380
My friend was an expert evaluator there.

115
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:41,980
I...

116
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,120
I just went to the restroom

117
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:46,040
to say hi to her,

118
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:50,420
and she stuffed cash into my hands right there.

119
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:53,540
I betrayed my loyalty and my original aspiration.

120
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:57,840
I let down the organization that nurtured me.

121
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:04,100
We experts have a group chat.

122
00:05:04,400 --> 00:05:07,800
Whoever gets picked posts a code word in the chat,

123
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:11,220
and those with connections refer clients.

124
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:15,360
After all, being an evaluator is a rare chance.

125
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:17,220
We...

126
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:20,260
we were actively looking to be bought off.

127
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,360
I abandoned my principles

128
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,420
and corrupted the business environment.

129
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,100
I'm sorry.

130
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,720
I'm so sorry.

131
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:34,860
The Discipline and Inspection Committee called in many experts recently.

132
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,760
Looks like

133
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:40,860
we'll have to call in the gods, too.

134
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,960
For a five-billion project,

135
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,820
someone's bound to be more anxious than us.

136
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:55,300
Then I'll go burn incense right now.

137
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:04,700
Team Leader,

138
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:05,400
here is what I compiled:

139
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,680
the interview records of all the experts.

140
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:14,680
The illicit tactics these experts used

141
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:16,700
are incredibly diverse.

142
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:18,580
There are way too many of them.

143
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:20,700
Team Leader,

144
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,440
Cyber Security just notified us

145
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,000
that there's movement on Du Qingbo's end.

146
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:24,960
They're making a move.

147
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:27,080
Bomb!

148
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:29,780
How's that?

149
00:06:29,980 --> 00:06:30,940
Can you beat it?

150
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,140
Pass.

151
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,100
Steel plate!

152
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:39,660
Secretary Tao, your hand is way too good!

153
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:40,200
How...

154
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:41,480
How are we supposed to play against that?

155
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,780
Keep going, Secretary Tao!

156
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,240
Go straight for the win!

157
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:48,020
Don't give them a chance to catch their breath!

158
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:48,700
You bet.

159
00:06:49,660 --> 00:06:51,740
Mr. Du, I'm a straight shooter.

160
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,460
Wheat is only harvested once a year.

161
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,920
If we don't harvest in time,

162
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,540
it'll rot in the field.

163
00:06:58,340 --> 00:06:59,700
Straight flush!

164
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:02,300
Straight flush!

165
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:03,340
That's right. How about that?

166
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:05,580
You think a straight flush is unbeatable?

167
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:08,040
I've got another bomb.

168
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:08,800
Bomb again!

169
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,180
Six Queens!

170
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:12,420
Take the lead, take the lead!

171
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:13,920
Then...

172
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:15,300
consecutive pairs!

173
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:16,840
We win!

174
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,220
A great omen! How auspicious!

175
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:22,860
Auspicious indeed!

176
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:23,860
Very auspicious!

177
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,160
A wonderful sign!

178
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:28,220
We've been sweating over this for three and a half years.

179
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,820
Just harvesting wheat won't cut it.

180
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,460
We deserve the full grand banquet.

181
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:33,020
Exactly.

182
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,020
Absolutely.

183
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,320
The grand banquet!

184
00:07:35,460 --> 00:07:36,380
Come on, come on.

185
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:37,460
Shuffle, shuffle!

186
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:37,840
Keep playing.

187
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,560
The client unit,

188
00:07:41,740 --> 00:07:43,340
the bidding agency,

189
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:45,080
the contractor...

190
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:50,120
Man.

191
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:53,380
Not a single one is missing.

192
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:57,160
For such a massive project,

193
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:00,820
you guys really went all out.

194
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:06,840
All checked off.

195
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:09,620
As for Mr. Lu...

196
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:11,140
Though he has deep pockets,

197
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:12,880
it's still a private enterprise.

198
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:15,760
On the surface, it needs proper packaging

199
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,420
to look legitimate.

200
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:19,060
Don't worry, there's a state-owned enterprise.

201
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:21,420
Jianzhou No. 3 Construction.

202
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,460
A joint bid.

203
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:24,380
A joint bid works,

204
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:25,740
but

205
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,700
we can't let them take too big a cut.

206
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,780
Isn't the Discipline and Inspection Committee

207
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:32,040
setting up nets and investigating everywhere?

208
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:36,220
Mr. Du, as a master of bidding and tendering,

209
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,580
what should we do next?

210
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:40,200
You have to show us the way.

211
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,000
Then we'll

212
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,100
serve them a few more dishes.

213
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:46,000
Keep them occupied.

214
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:48,900
That way, we can fish in troubled waters.

215
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,280
The Guangming Community Renovation Project bid evaluation

216
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,420
begins now.

217
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,440
No signs of intrusion were found,

218
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:09,680
nor any Trojans.

219
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:11,900
No hacker breach,

220
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:13,220
and no Trojan programs.

221
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:15,900
Then what kind of game are they playing?

222
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:17,420
Either way, as for the experts,

223
00:09:17,420 --> 00:09:18,660
they won't be able to bypass them.

224
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,720
They must have another angle.

225
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,380
Check it again thoroughly.

226
00:09:44,140 --> 00:09:44,940
Hello?

227
00:09:45,940 --> 00:09:46,740
Yes, Chief.

228
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:49,380
It must be the check-in system.

229
00:09:49,780 --> 00:09:51,740
They definitely installed new equipment recently.

230
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:54,740
Facial recognition.

231
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:56,920
I don't know much about software,

232
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,040
but I know the hardware when I see it.

233
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,980
My colleague told me

234
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,500
there's an expensive cracking software.

235
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,300
As soon as an expert checks in,

236
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,560
the system automatically

237
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,700
sends their info to their inbox.

238
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,220
Then they assign people

239
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,700
to approach them one-on-one.

240
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,520
If that's true,

241
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:15,520
they really spent a fortune.

242
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,080
Chief,

243
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,400
this counts as major meritorious service, right?
